OL,3,GNEWSATown's 347-year-old clock to chime
OL,4,Aagain
OL,5,
OL,6,FA council has pledged to repair a
OL,7,Ftown's 347-year-old clock which has not
OL,8,Fchimed in a decade.
OL,10,FJack White, a councillor on Watton Town
OL,11,FCouncil, said the process was "under
OL,12,Fway" to restore the tower and clock on
OL,13,Fthe town's High Street in Norfolk,
OL,14,Fwhich were built in 1679.
OL,16,FMore than #20,000 has been spent on
OL,17,Fservicing and repairing the clock in
OL,18,Fthe past 15 years, said resident Sandra
OL,19,FOsborn, who has been calling for the
OL,20,Frestoration.
OL,23,APub: 27-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
